  "reason": "With only two completed experiments, evidence is very sparse. RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) at 0.485 acc clearly outperforms image (resnet50, singleprofile) at 0.208 acc, making RNA the dominant modality and its representation the most critical design choice to understand. Config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001: only the RNA encoder changes (pca_n2000 → scvi_n200), while profile setting, modality, and all other settings remain identical. This isolates whether a learned generative representation (scVI) can outperform a linear PCA projection, directly informing whether we should invest in more sophisticated encoders for all downstream multimodal experiments. Under a tight budget, resolving whether the RNA representation is the bottleneck before adding complexity (multiprofile, aggregation, fusion) is the highest-information next step."
}

